id: pm-x8jdt8
title: "GH-1351: leaf get advertises empty children as omitted"
description: A full get/read/show of a leaf item marks children omitted despite zero children; the suggested follow-up returns an empty rollup. Correct materiality in the SDK without hiding populated children or notes.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T14:54:09.941Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-30T05:20:31.250Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-30T05:20:30.508Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-30T05:20:30.508Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Real isolated tracker proves a parent with one child and a leaf with zero children across get, show, and read; full leaf reads have no empty children omission; populated omitted children retain recovery guidance; previously repaired notes behavior remains correct; Task parents retain child recovery in standard, brief, and deep reads; Both explicit full spellings return the child rollup for every type while full leaves remain complete"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "SDK full reads compute child materiality for every type, complete receipts strictly report false/zero/empty, and ordinary Task reads retain child recovery without corpus enumeration. CLI get/show/read full aliases preserve notes and SDK semantics."
expected_result: Leaves and parents expose truthful complete receipts while routine Task reads remain bounded and omitted children remain recoverable.
actual_result: "Focused SDK/Bun/CLI 14/14 pass on the updated 2026.9.30 build and both previously linked commands pass; an isolated real production mutation passes the old SDK assertion and fails both strengthened boundary assertions. Full source coverage passes 9434 tests, two platform skips, exact 100/100/100/100 across 758 unchanged sources. Packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx prove changed parent behavior and previous data compatibility. Current reviewed b449ce52f protected checks all passed; the version-only 2026.9.30 baseline plus tracker closure will receive fresh checks/reviews before merge. Separate disclosed timing/runtime/documentation/telemetry gaps remain unresolved; publication is not claimed."
